WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.569
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing 12 more incredible

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:10.219
easter eggs you might have missed in Toy Story
4 including one which may break the entire

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:11.219
Pixar Theory!

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:16.049
And we also have an answer from Pixar on whether
this really is Boo from Monsters Inc!

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.900
I'll be discussing a few spoilers, so take
care if you haven't seen the new movie yet.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.130
My giveaway is still running, so subscribe,
hit the bell and let me know your thoughts

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.579
about Toy Story 4 for a chance to win.

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:30.750
We're kicking off this list with a breakdown
of the opening flashback where there's a number

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.300
of intriguing easter eggs and Toy Story call-backs.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.430
As RC's rescue gets underway, look carefully
at the cover of the book that Molly's dolls

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.070
give Bo Peep and you'll see a little unicorn
with a rainbow mane and tail.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:47.190
That's a nod to Rainbow Unicorn, one of the
actresses who worked at Dream Productions

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.410
in Inside Out.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.440
"She wants your autograph."

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.920
"No, no, Sadness, don't bother Miss Unicorn,
okay?"

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.550
"Sorry, she's from out of town."

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.720
And when Woody is using Slinky to try and
reach RC, he finds he can't get near enough,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.320
until the Barrel of Monkeys come to the rescue
and give him the extra length he finally needs

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.890
to grab hold of the remote control car.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.649
This is a nice call-back to the first movie
where the toys were trying to rescue Buzz

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:11.920
but the monkeys couldn't reach far enough.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.280
"It's too short!

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.090
We need more monkeys!"

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.359
"Buzz, the monkeys aren't working!

00:01:17.359 --> 00:01:19.179
We're formulating another plan!"

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:24.260
This opening scene in Toy Story 4 also fills
us in on how Bo Peep ended up separated from

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.260
the other toys.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.850
And the car she's taken away in has an incredible
Pixar easter egg on its licence plate which

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.689
reads "RMR F97".

00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:36.600
If you're scratching your head about this
cryptic combo of numbers and letters, well,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.170
it's the Unix computer command which somebody
at Pixar ran in 1997 and which accidentally

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:46.500
deleted the whole of Toy Story 2 from Pixar's
servers.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.659
The movie was only saved because one of Pixar's
employees who was on maternity leave at the

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:54.700
time had taken a backup of the movie home
with her about a month earlier.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.909
Toy Story 4's filmmakers said that they "thought
it was appropriate somehow that the licence

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:03.670
plate on the car that takes Bo away almost
killed Toy Story 2."

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.289
And as the flashback ends and the Toy Story
4 title comes on screen, the camera pans up

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:13.390
to a blue sky filled with clouds in a nostalgic
call-back to how the first Toy Story opened

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:18.220
with Andy holding up Woody against the blue
sky and white cloud wallpaper in Andy's room.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.650
The orange, white, and black design on the
swim ring we see Bonnie wearing as she plays

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:27.480
with her toys is a delightful easter egg to
the clownfish Nemo from the movies Finding

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.120
Nemo and Finding Dory.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.470
When Bonnie goes to kindergarten, look out
for an easter egg on the lunchbox that Woody

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.700
hides behind.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.700
On the box, there's a picture of Reptillus
Maximus from the Toy Story TV special Toy

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.920
Story That Time Forgot.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.390
"What fearsome dinosaurs are these?"

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.390
"Oh?!"

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.019
"Greetings, I am Reptillus Maximus."

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:51.420
And it's in Bonnie's classroom where we get
the first possible appearance of Boo in Toy

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.420
Story 4.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.140
Ever since the trailer for the movie dropped,
fans have wondered if this is Boo from Monsters

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.140
Inc.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.510
Later promotional material gives us a much
better look at this girl and I have to say

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.750
she does look an awful lot like Boo.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:07.150
Boo also seems to make another appearance
later in the film at the carnival game booth

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.620
where Buzz ends up with Ducky and Bunny.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.890
One of the girls playing the game has Boo's
characteristic look and many fans have also

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.620
said they think it's Boo.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.900
On my other Toy Story 4 easter eggs video,
"The Criticizer" commented that in the carnival

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.799
scene Boo tries to win a prize but loses and
when she looks at the carnival worker he doesn't

00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:25.799
care.

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:30.310
Now, if Boo really is in Toy Story 4, then
what does that mean for the timeline established

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.950
in the Pixar Theory?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.269
Just in case you're unfamiliar, there are
a number of Pixar theories around, but the

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:40.849
best-known one is by Jon Negroni who has suggested
a unified timeline for all the Pixar films.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:45.560
In Negroni's Pixar theory, Monsters Inc is
supposed to take place well into the future,

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.920
several thousand years after the Toy Story
movies, but if Boo is here in Toy Story 4,

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.030
how can that be?

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:56.300
Well, the theory says that the monsters in
Monsters Inc are travelling back in time when

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:01.060
they open doors to visit children, so Boo
could be growing up alongside Bonnie and getting

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.350
visits from Sully at the same time.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:07.129
It also makes me wonder if any of these monsters
visited Andy or Bonnie.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:12.659
However, in an attempt to put people's Boo-related
theories to rest, one of Toy Story's producers,

00:04:12.659 --> 00:04:15.030
Jonas Rivera, has weighed in on the matter.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.889
In an interview with Digital Spy the filmmaker
said the following:

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:20.680
"I looked at her again, but it wasn't her.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.120
Maybe I should just say it's Boo, but it's
not Boo.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.190
I don't think we could even use the model
of Boo, it's so old, but we do love Boo.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:29.970
It's just a kid that looks like her."

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:33.090
Let me know what you think in the comments
below.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.699
Now we need to talk more about the Pixar theory
as there's an easter egg that Toy Story 4's

00:04:37.699 --> 00:04:41.650
director Josh Cooley deliberately added to
the movie in reference to it.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:42.650
Just in case you're unfamiliar, there are
a number of Pixar theories around, but the

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.650
best-known one is by Jon Negroni who has suggested
a unified timeline for all the Pixar films.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.720
In an interview with JoBlo, Cooley said that
in the scene where Bonnie and her family are

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.419
at the RV park, her mum is sitting outside
reading a book titled "Beyond Infinity: Debunking

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:53.450
Theories of a Shared Universe".

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:57.520
Cooley didn't say whether he was just poking
fun at the Pixar Theory with this easter egg

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.390
or was purposely trying to debunk it.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:04.370
However, it is interesting that in the final
cut of Toy Story 4, the director decided to

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.990
change the angle of the shot so that the title
of the book was obscured, though he says he

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.509
did that because it was "too distracting for
the audience."

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:15.860
So whether all the easter eggs we love to
talk about in Pixar movies actually add up

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.979
to a fully-connected shared universe is still
up for debate and in some ways Toy Story 4

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:26.000
does confirm some aspects of the Pixar theory
even if it raises other questions.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.240
One part of the theory is that toys come to
life thanks to the energy they feed off children's

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.340
emotions, and when Toy Story 4 introduces
Forky, he's really confused about why he's

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.340
alive.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.340
"Why am I alive?"

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:41.610
"You're Bonnie's toy, you are going to help
create happy memories that will last for the

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.550
rest of her life."

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:47.960
On one hand, the fact that Bonnie created
and then loved Forky seems to confirm the

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.470
Pixar theory idea that a toy comes to life
from the energy they receive from a child's

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:58.350
emotions.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:02.729
But there's still that moment in the mid-credits
scene where Forky meets a new cutlery soulmate

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.919
who when she asks "How am I alive?"

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:06.789
Forky replies "I don't know".

00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:11.389
In fact, Toy Story 4's filmmakers deliberately
added this scene with Forky in order to have

00:06:11.389 --> 00:06:14.180
what they've called a "get out of jail free
card".

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:19.120
In an interview with Digital Spy, Josh Cooley
said "Part of me doesn't want to try and answer

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.389
all the magic of [why toys are alive].

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:26.099
In Forky's case, Bonnie has given him a new
purpose, but that's not always the case where

00:06:26.099 --> 00:06:28.979
toys haven't had kids and are still alive."

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:34.160
There are dozens more easter eggs in Toy Story
4 which you might have missed including A113,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.180
the Pizza Planet Truck, and the Luxo Ball,
all of which are hidden in the antique store

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.479
and the carnival.

